<!--
---
description: "Research-study version of the Psychology Study Group: the course, preceded by the University of Memphis informed-consent form. Students may take part in the study or not; the course is identical either way, and the answer can be changed at any time from Study Consent Form at the bottom of the course navigation. For the course without the study, launch psych_course."
category: psychology
index: -1
lang: en-Latn-US
license: AGPL
---
-->

<!--
  RESEARCH CONSENT GATE

  The research deployment's route "/" lands here, not on the course. Three
  states:
  * unanswered -> the IRB form
  * answered but not acknowledged -> a short, neutral acknowledgment with
    the practical notes about the platform
  * acknowledged -> the course itself

  The gates test ANSWERED, never the value: declining changes nothing about
  what the student does, and the activity carries the same credit. The
  acknowledgment reads differently for the two answers only in its heading;
  the notes and the button are the same.

  The same form block is also the last child of the course (one block, one
  state), so a student can revisit it and change their answer at any time.
  Revisiting shows the form and the choice only; the acknowledgment is a
  one-time landing step, not part of the form.

  The course itself stays launchable, so the same content serves outside a
  study with no wrapper at all. Which consent-form version a student saw is
  recoverable from the release the event log ties back to.
-->

<Vertical id="psych_study" title="Psychology Study Group (Research Study)" launchable="true">

<Use ref="psych_irb_consent_form" when="!@psych_irb_consent.value" />

<Vertical id="psych_irb_ack" when="@psych_irb_consent.value && !@psych_irb_ack_done.value">
<Markdown when="@psych_irb_consent.value === 'consented'">
## Thank you

Your course work may be included in the research, always de-identified. You
can change your answer at any time under **Study Consent Form** at the bottom
of the course navigation.
</Markdown>
<Markdown when="@psych_irb_consent.value === 'declined'">
## No problem

Your course work stays out of the research. Nothing about the course changes:
same activities, same credit. You can change your answer at any time under
**Study Consent Form** at the bottom of the course navigation.
</Markdown>
<Markdown>
This SBLA Activity is a requirement for our course, and you will receive
points for completing it whether or not you consent to having your data
included in the research.

This is an **experimental, open-source research platform**, and you are
among the first students to use it. A few notes:

* We recommend Firefox, Edge, or Google Chrome. Safari is unsupported.
* We recommend against working on multiple devices at the same time.
* If you run into any issues, even minor, please let us know. You'll
  be helping out future students.
</Markdown>
<ActionButton id="psych_irb_ack_btn" label="Continue to the Study Group">
<SetFieldAction id="psych_irb_ack_set" target="psych_irb_ack_done" field="value" value="acknowledged" />
</ActionButton>
</Vertical>

<Use ref="psych_course" when="@psych_irb_consent.value && @psych_irb_ack_done.value" />

<!-- Flag holder for the acknowledgment, parked unrendered. A LineInput, not
     a Done: SetFieldAction validates against the target field's schema, and
     a plain string can say what happened. -->
<Hidden id="psych_consent_defs">
<LineInput id="psych_irb_ack_done" />
</Hidden>

</Vertical> <!-- psych_study -->
